  "source_gate": "SD",
  "reason": "CD+Tests exposed a design gap: the approved SDD-01/SDD-04 rule treats any stored-versus-evaluated gate difference as stale. An existing safety test (packages/core/test/artefact-recording-test.js:254-258) requires that a run whose evaluated gate moved backward after evidence was retracted (stored QA, CD+Tests reset to missing) does not start automatic implementation. The approved rule would start it.",
  "intended_change": "Revise SDD-01 and SDD-04 to a forward-only rule: the stored next step is stale only when the run is active and the evaluated gate lies after the stored gate in the canonical gate order; a backward or unknown stored gate keeps the stored text (fail closed). The observed defect (stored Brownfield Analysis, evaluated CD+Tests) is a forward move and stays fixed; PRD AC-003 already specifies the earlier-gate case. TP scenarios add the backward case.",
